From edad7c44f01c6020eb9540c0aa6b48e5d098ce87 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: beau4201 <beau.ten.berge@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 17:00:45 +0100
Subject: [PATCH 17/18] oblivios: stop the warm decoy with delayed locking so
 its CE key stays resident

The plain stop evicted the decoy's CE key 0.2 s after every owner unlock, so the lock-time start could only reach RUNNING_LOCKED and the decoy launcher started cold after the duress credential (3 s black screen, DUR-019). The decoy user type allows delayed locking, so the key now stays resident and the next warm start unlocks at once.
---
 .../server/locksettings/DecoyProfileHelper.java        | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/services/core/java/com/android/server/locksettings/DecoyProfileHelper.java b/services/core/java/com/android/server/locksettings/DecoyProfileHelper.java
index 91d81af6..79aef4cd 100644
--- a/services/core/java/com/android/server/locksettings/DecoyProfileHelper.java
+++ b/services/core/java/com/android/server/locksettings/DecoyProfileHelper.java
@@ -177,7 +177,7 @@ class DecoyProfileHelper {
      *   <li>Independently, even if that reasoning were ever wrong: the current-foreground-user
      *       check below refuses to stop the target if it is the current user, and
      *       UserController#stopUsersLU -- the real code eventually reached through
-     *       IActivityManager#stopUserWithCallback below -- unconditionally refuses to stop
+     *       IActivityManager#stopUserWithDelayedLocking below -- unconditionally refuses to stop
      *       whichever user is currently in the foreground (returns USER_OP_IS_CURRENT) as a
      *       built-in AOSP safety check, not something this class relies on being correct on its
      *       own.
@@ -209,7 +209,13 @@ class DecoyProfileHelper {
             }
             IActivityManager am = ActivityManager.getService();
             try {
-                am.stopUserWithCallback(state.decoyUserId, /* callback= */ null);
+                // ObliviOS: delayed locking, not the plain stop. The plain stop evicts the decoy's CE
+                // key within 0.2 s, so the next lock-time start can only reach RUNNING_LOCKED and the
+                // decoy launcher starts cold after the duress credential (3 s of black, DUR-019). The
+                // decoy user type allows delayed locking (frameworks-base/0001), so the key stays
+                // resident and the next warm start unlocks at once; the storage holds only decoy
+                // data. Removing the decoy removes the user and its key with it (DUR-007).
+                am.stopUserWithDelayedLocking(state.decoyUserId, /* callback= */ null);
             } catch (RemoteException e) {
                 Slog.w(TAG, "Failed to stop unused warm-started credential-routing target", e);
             }
